# The `*` rule at the bottom is deliberate: it makes the infrastructure
# team the repository code owner, so GitHub requests the team for review.
# Merge gating by code owners additionally requires the
# `require_code_owner_review` ruleset setting (currently off).
#
# The /test slash command (.github/workflows/slash-test.yml) reads the
# `/test allowlist:` line below from the default branch and authorizes only
# the listed users:
# the commenter, the PR author, and (for fork PRs) the fork owner must
# all appear there. GitHub Actions cannot read team membership
# (GITHUB_TOKEN is repository-scoped and has no organization Members
# permission), so the team has to be listed explicitly; a team handle
# cannot be expanded by the workflow.
